WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
Hey, welcome to Planetarian Daily, episode 89.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.080
Today is June 14th, 2026.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.240
Let's get into today's research and health developments.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.300
The week's biggest developments pulled together

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.960
what actually moved, why it matters,

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.280
and what to watch next.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.640
An integration of 140 studies shows consistent links

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.860
between lower socioeconomic status,

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.460
discrimination exposure, and faster epigenetic aging

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.840
across nearly 66,000 people.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.580
The effects appear independent of other measured variables

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.600
and converge on measurable shifts

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.380
in biological aging markers.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:40.980
Lower socioeconomic status aligned with consistent shifts

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.980
in cortical organization that appeared independent

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.400
of other measured variables.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.900
Discrimination exposure tied to faster epigenetic aging

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.080
in patterns that held after adjustment

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.300
for multiple health and behavioral factors.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:58.340
The work draws on repeated measures across large cohorts

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:02.120
to map how social conditions alter biological aging clocks.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.640
Engineers constructed gold-based metamaterials

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.600
that increased energy flow across nanoscale gaps

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.660
by up to four times compared with conventional materials.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.760
The structures exploit near-field radiative heat transfer

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.340
that conventional theory predicts should be limited

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.280
at these scales.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.000
Measurements confirm the enhancement held

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.480
across multiple gap distances and material configurations.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.080
The result challenges assumptions

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.360
about thermal transport limits in miniaturized systems.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.160
Applications under investigation include chip-level cooling

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.940
and compact energy devices.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:40.220
Researchers developed a solar-driven material

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:43.580
that uses one photon to drive two linked reactions.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.200
The catalyst simultaneously reduces carbon dioxide

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.380
and oxidizes organic waste,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:52.220
yielding useful chemicals from both streams.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.180
The approach avoids separate energy inputs

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.560
for each half reaction.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:00.660
Performance data shows stable operation under visible light

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.740
without precious metal co-catalists.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.580
Next steps include scaling the material

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.360
for continuous flow reactors.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.480
From population-level drivers of aging

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.060
to a first in human test of whether cellular aging itself

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.600
can be reversed in tissue.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.480
Life biosciences administered partial cellular

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.160
reprogramming therapy to a glaucoma patient

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.080
targeting retinal ganglion cell regeneration.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.260
The approach resets epigenetic age

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.800
while avoiding full pluripotent conversion

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.240
to reduce tumor risk.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.580
Early safety monitoring will track the injected eye

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:36.720
over the coming months.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.400
The treatment aims to regenerate retinal ganglion cells

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.220
by resetting epigenetic age in nerve tissue.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.480
Partial reprogramming was chosen specifically

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:49.020
to limit the risk of uncontrolled cell growth.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.800
An aridomized trial of people with type 2 diabetes,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.640
an SGLT2 inhibitor produced an over 80% reduction

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.640
in heart failure hospitalizations

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.380
among carriers of pathogenic cardiomyopathy variants.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:06.640
Exome sequencing performed after the trial

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.340
identified the genetic subgroup.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.200
The Kaplan-myer curve showed separation

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.920
between treatment and placebo arms in this subset.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.440
The finding points to genotype-specific responses

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.040
already captured in existing trial datasets.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.440
Aranomized trial tested a myostatin inhibitor alongside

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:28.240
terzepotide in adults receiving the GLP1 agonist.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:32.980
Participants on the combination retained 55% more lean mass

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:35.580
than those on placebo plus terzepotide.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.340
The study supplies proof of concept

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:41.300
that blocking myostatin can offset muscle loss

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.420
during weight reduction.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.360
Follow-up work will test longer durations

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.140
and functional strength measures.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:50.660
Higher adherence to a Mediterranean eating pattern

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.240
correlated with elevated circulating levels

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:55.700
of the mitochondrial derived peptides,

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.720
huminin and SHM OES.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.460
Olive oil, fish, and legumes showed the strongest

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:03.900
food level associations.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.100
Human and levels also tracked inversely

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.060
with two oxidative stress markers.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.400
The observational data suggests these peptides

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.440
may link dietary patterns to mitochondrial function.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.300
From attempts to reset aging in the eye,

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:21.080
to new clues about how aging-related inflammation

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.740
is controlled inside brain immune cells.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.220
Researchers identified an epigenetic regulator

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.640
that alters mitochondrial function inside microglia

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.300
and drives their pro-inflammatory state.

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:36.580
The pro-inflammatory state of microglia

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.960
drives disease progression

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.740
in experimental models of Alzheimer's disease.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.140
Targeting the regulator offers a potential route

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.720
to modify disease progression in those models.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.880
The regulator acts directly on mitochondria

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.240
within the brain's resident immune cells.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.020
Work remains at the pre-clinical stage

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.580
with tests now focused on whether blocking

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:59.960
the regulator reduces inflammation markers.

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:03.660
From microglial mechanisms in neurodegeneration

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.760
to another basic finding on how the brain switches

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.200
between behavioral states.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.800
Specific neural signals were shown to control the shift

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.360
from one habitual behavior to another in mice.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.260
The signals provide a mechanistic window

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.920
into behavioral flexibility at the circuit level.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.280
Optogenetic manipulation of the identified neurons

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:26.020
produced rapid switches between learned routines.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.780
The work isolates a discrete population of cells

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:33.200
whose activity determines when one habit gives way to the next.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:35.920
From habit circuits to a separate manipulation

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.120
that mimic sleep's effects on memory.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.620
Stimulating defined brain activity patterns in a wake mice

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.000
produce memory gains comparable to natural deep sleep.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.540
The stimulation isolates the physiological features

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.480
responsible for sleep-dependent memory consolidation.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:56.960
Memory performance improved on hippocampal dependent tasks

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.280
after the targeted patterns were delivered

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.200
during wakefulness.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.260
The result shows that specific oscillatory activity

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.220
rather than sleep itself drives the consolidation benefit.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:12.280
Scores rose in women later diagnosed with breast cancer.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:14.720
Elevation appeared up to 10 years

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.060
before clinical detection in the retrospective analysis.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.920
A separate perspective study supports the pattern

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.880
over a three to five year window.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.960
The approach uses standard mammogram reads

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.180
already performed by radiologists.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.300
Validation in larger cohorts is the next reported step.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:38.220
Analysis of 264,000 pregnancies over 20 years

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:42.060
found no elevated risk of major congenital anomalies

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:45.580
after exposure to paracetamol or common NSAIDs.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.100
The study drew on linked prescription

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.460
and birth registry data across multiple health systems.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:55.320
Researchers compared exposed and unexposed pregnancies

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:57.120
while controlling from maternal age,

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.180
smoking, and other medications.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:02.480
Results align with earlier smaller studies

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.620
but carry greater statistical power.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.760
Regulators and clinicians can use the data

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.220
when updating prenatal pain management guidance.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:13.860
From acute memory mechanisms to longer term

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:16.060
nutritional associations with brain health.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.520
In over 2,000 adults over age 64,

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.720
higher circulating vitamin C corresponded

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:24.320
to larger gray matter volumes

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:26.940
and stronger default mode network connections.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:29.960
The associations held after adjustment

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.740
for diet quality and education.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.580
Plasma measurements came from a single

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.300
fasting sample per participant.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.300
The default mode network supports attention

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:43.340
and autobiographical memory, both vulnerable in aging.

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:46.620
Researchers plan longitudinal follow-up

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.000
to test whether raising vitamin C intake

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.460
slows network decline.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.540
From nutrient associations and aging brains

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.000
to early life environmental influences

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.640
on later emotional health.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:01.580
More outdoor play between ages 2 and 4 correlated

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:04.380
with reduced emotional and behavioral problems

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:08.320
by age 8 after socioeconomic and screen time adjustments.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.720
Each additional outdoor day per week

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.240
raised the odds of healthy mental health scores.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.660
The analysis drew on repeated behavioral assessments

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.760
across early and middle childhood.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:23.160
Researchers adjusted for socioeconomic status,

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:26.500
screen time, and parental mental health in the models.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:29.280
The study followed children longitudinal

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.540
from preschool into middle childhood.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:35.100
Researchers developed culture dog muscle cells

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.220
that allow early testing of new treatments

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.960
before animal studies begin.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:42.120
The cells retain key functional properties

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:45.600
of native canine muscle and respond to candidate compounds

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:46.960
in predictable ways.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:50.300
This platform reduces the number of dogs needed

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:52.760
for initial safety and efficacy checks.

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:56.220
The approach supplies a standardized starting point

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:59.800
for identifying which molecules merit further investigation.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.880
The method infers protein sequences

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.560
by tracing evolutionary history backward.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.300
It targets enzymes that may have performed optimally

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.500
millions of years ago.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:12.760
Researchers apply the technique

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:16.300
when modern versions fall short for biotechnology needs.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.880
The approach reconstructs sequences computationally

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:21.300
before laboratory testing.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.700
No specific performance metrics appear in the post.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.940
Before we go, keep an eye on early data

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:30.340
from in vivo gene editing trials

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.740
that could clarify safety profiles

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:34.700
for one shot hereditary treatments.

